  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## [3.2.0.2] - 2026-11-18\n\n### Added\n\n- Flags on pairing list entries to indicate whether a device is paired via Bluetooth LE, Classic or both.\n- Connection type on `IBluetoothChildDevice` to indicate whether the device is connected via Bluetooth LE or Classic.\n- Possibility to specify the desired Bluetooth type when connecting to a device, when the device is paired via both Bluetooth LE and Classic.\n- Documentation on how how to let the dongle scan for devices until explicitly stopped, instead of stopping automatically after a timeout.\n\n### Changed \n\n- The module is now licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- An issue where LE-only devices would cause pairing to fail.\n- An issue where a slow setup of the dongle-device connection could cause the SDK to report the pairing as failed when it actually succeeded.",
